    "result_text": "The build is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an `initials` field to the owner API response, returning the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\n**Changes (2 files):**\n\n1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 declared a read-only `initials` string property on the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field).\n2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method, mirroring the neighbouring `displayName` idiom:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I deliberately reused the existing MapStruct expression pattern rather than adding a method to the `Person` model. That keeps the derivation a single CC-1 line inside the already-simple mapper interface (low `WMC_other`), and touches only 2 files instead of 3 \u2014 the schema plus one mapper annotation, no growth of any method or class.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
